{
  "id": "s03-l04",
  "unit": "s03-vowel-signs",
  "title": "Vowel signs 4: ো ৌ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**These signs wrap around the consonant.** ো is ে on the left plus া on the right: কো = `ko`. Find the consonant in the middle, then read *one* vowel `o`: ভালো (`bhalo`), তোমার (`tomar`), বোন (`bon`), ছোট (`chhoto`).\n\n**ৌ** is the same wrap but with a curly tail (ৗ) on the right instead of the stick: `ou` as in *low*. নৌকা (`nouka`, *boat*), মৌমাছি (`moumachhi`, *bee*).\n\n**Don't read it as e + a.** কো never means *kea*. Whenever ে and া hug one letter, it's ো.\n\nRecap of sign positions: right (া ী), left (ি ে ৈ), below (ু ূ ৃ), both sides (ো ৌ).",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "k-o",
      "bn": "কো",
      "tr": "ko",
      "en": "ো (o-kar): adds 'o' as in 'go'; wraps around the consonant",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ো (U+09CB; canonically ে U+09C7 + া U+09BE, stored precomposed here per NFC). Name o-kar (ও-কার)."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-ou",
      "bn": "কৌ",
      "tr": "kou",
      "en": "ৌ (ou-kar): adds 'ou' as in 'low'; wraps around the consonant",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ৌ (U+09CC; ে + ৗ U+09D7, stored precomposed per NFC). Name ou-kar (ঔ-কার)."
    },
    {
      "id": "nouka",
      "bn": "নৌকা",
      "tr": "nouka",
      "en": "boat"
    },
    {
      "id": "moumachhi",
      "bn": "মৌমাছি",
      "tr": "moumachhi",
      "en": "bee",
      "notes": "মৌ = honey (poetic), মাছি = fly."
    }
  ],
